of political and economic uncertainty. Germany is seeking alternative partners in the region, but also wants good ties with Beijing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Remark on Modi's father stirs political row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76b3b01106bb258890bca38a2be4426960451dd63381c0ff481ef9677de2c13c</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:19:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T07:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-remark-on-modi-s-father-stirs-political-row/live-79758965--7e6cacdc5195.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-remark-on-modi-s-father-stirs-political-row/live-79758965?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An opposition leader's impromptu remark concerning PM Modi is causing a political stir in India with the ruling party now planning a protest. Also, the prince of Liechtenstein is in Mumbai. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rahul Gandhi urges protest against voter deletions, announces November 1 rally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c8e8edf2193685d7362c1ea9ef9cd75608bee18e28cd145291a6908eb402817</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-urges-protest-against-voter-deletions-announces-november-1-rally/live-79748098--c4b74d8129c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-urges-protest-against-voter-deletions-announces-november-1-rally/live-79748098?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's opposition leader Rahul Gandhi has accused the ruling BJP of "vote theft" and urged people to join a rally in Delhi on November 1. The call comes amid protests over revision of electoral rolls. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Russia's arrest of Japanese journalist is the latest sign of deteriorating ties between the countries.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11c6ec277e6244942a819695ece1f5f33e32e34bcea49b15d1d177397a1773d3</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-coun/a-79742995--e6439f04b25d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-countries/a-79742995?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan is demanding access to a journalist who was arrested by Russian security services. The Kremlin claims that Japan is using journalists as spies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb241807f107024ba74b3825f2aa8948b0e8328bc317d645f513c3383d45ef0b</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877--83771c04f78a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a9c40dd754703cd229bef7547028e2825ba7893d4758eaa415a4ea4bd45cd7</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a6a61174d241e9be2370cee6bcba64de1ea54653965ea96e3c4c51802b9b54</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f5fd316c9435e792a015903c08688e39ead8b329e23ca575e4ef277dcc70625</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
